    {"t":1,"a":"SGWN","n":"MacRitchie Reservoir & TreeTop Walk","address":"MacRitchie Reservoir Park, Lornie Road","k":"Nature","w":"Central Catchment rainforest reservoir with a 250 m suspension bridge, 25 m up in the forest canopy.","sources":[["NPARKS","https://www.nparks.gov.sg/visit/parks/central-catchment-nature-reserve/activities/hiking-nature-walk"],["WIKI","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MacRitchie_Reservoir"]]},
    {"t":2,"a":"SGWN","n":"Bukit Timah Nature Reserve","address":"177 Hindhede Drive, Bukit Timah","k":"Nature","w":"ASEAN Heritage Park protecting primary rainforest and Singapore's highest natural point (163 m).","sources":[["NPARKS","https://www.nparks.gov.sg/visit/parks/park-detail/bukit-timah-nature-reserve"],["WIKI","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bukit_Timah_Nature_Reserve"]]},
    {"t":1,"a":"SGWN","n":"Singapore Zoo","address":"80 Mandai Lake Road, Mandai","k":"Wildlife","w":"World-renowned open-concept zoo of over 4,200 animals in naturalistic, cage-free habitats.","sources":[["MANDAI","https://www.mandai.com/en/singapore-zoo.html"],["WIKI","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singapore_Zoo"]]},
    {"t":1,"a":"SGWN","n":"Night Safari","address":"80 Mandai Lake Road, Mandai","k":"Wildlife","w":"The world's first nocturnal zoo (1994); tram rides through 35 hectares of after-dark habitats.","sources":[["MANDAI","https://www.mandai.com/en/night-safari.html"],["WIKI","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Safari,_Singapore"]]},
    {"t":2,"a":"SGWN","n":"River Wonders","address":"80 Mandai Lake Road, Mandai","k":"Wildlife","w":"Asia's only river-themed wildlife park, home to giant pandas and a giant Amazon river tank.","sources":[["MANDAI","https://www.mandai.com/en/river-wonders.html"],["WIKI","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Wonders"]]},
